IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 5A (further circumstances in which a claimant with limited capability for
-- work and work-related activity is a "pre-2026 claimant" for the purposes of regulation 27).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- WHY IT IS HERE. The brief's one-line description of this piece names Schedules 1 to 5; its line range (1821 to 2721) also takes in Schedule 5A,
-- lines 2696 to 2721, which no other piece owns, so it is encoded here.
--
-- DATES. Nothing in this range says when the Schedule comes into force: there is no commencement provision in the lines read. The one date it
-- names, 6th April 2026, is carried as a named constant with its own reference, and every paragraph tests against it. Whether a day is "before" it
-- is a plain comparison; a day "on or after" it is the opposite comparison.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as facts: regulation 27A(1) (piece uc1, the first circumstances in which a claimant is a "pre-2026 claimant"; regulation 27 reads the result), regulation 28(1) (the relevant period),
-- regulation 41(1)(a) and (b) (piece uc4, awaiting an assessment under Part 5).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The date the Schedule turns on.
-- src:2703 | (a) before 6th April 2026, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), the claimant is awaiting an assessment under Part 5, and
@ref Sch 5A para 2(1)(a) (src:2703)
GIVETH A DATE
`Sch 5A — 6th April 2026` MEANS YearMonthDay 2026 4 6

-- Paragraph 2: awaiting an assessment under Part 5 before 6th April 2026; determined to have LCWRA, and entitled to an LCWRA award, on or after it.
-- Sub-paragraph (2): the decision may be made on a revision, a supersession or an appeal; the route is irrelevant, and no rule reads it.
-- src:2702 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2703 | (a) before 6th April 2026, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), the claimant is awaiting an assessment under Part 5, and
-- src:2704 | (b) on or after 6th April 2026, the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element.
-- src:2705 | (2) The decision in sub-paragraph (1)(b), or paragraph 3(b), may be made on a revision of a decision under section 9 of the Social Security Act 1998, a supersession of a decision under section 10 of that Act, or on an appeal.
@ref Sch 5A para 2 (src:2702-2705)
DECLARE `Route by which a decision is made` IS ONE OF
    `a revision of a decision under section 9 of the Social Security Act 1998`
    `a supersession of a decision under section 10 of that Act`
    `an appeal`
    `some other route`

-- src:2702 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2703 | (a) before 6th April 2026, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), the claimant is awaiting an assessment under Part 5, and
-- src:2704 | (b) on or after 6th April 2026, the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element.
-- src:2705 | (2) The decision in sub-paragraph (1)(b), or paragraph 3(b), may be made on a revision of a decision under section 9 of the Social Security Act 1998, a supersession of a decision under section 10 of that Act, or on an appeal.
@ref Sch 5A para 2 (src:2702-2705)
DECLARE `Claimant awaiting an assessment under Part 5` HAS
    -- out of range: reg 41(1)(a) (piece uc4)
    `a day before 6th April 2026 on which, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), the claimant was awaiting an assessment under Part 5`  IS A DATE
    `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element`  IS A DATE
    `the route by which that decision is made`                                                                                                IS A `Route by which a decision is made`

-- src:2702 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2703 | (a) before 6th April 2026, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), the claimant is awaiting an assessment under Part 5, and
-- src:2704 | (b) on or after 6th April 2026, the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element.
@ref Sch 5A para 2(1) (src:2702-2704)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant awaiting an assessment under Part 5`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5A para 2 — the claimant was awaiting an assessment before 6th April 2026 and is determined to have LCWRA on or after it` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `a day before 6th April 2026 on which, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), the claimant was awaiting an assessment under Part 5` LESS THAN `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)
    AND (claimant's `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element` AT LEAST `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)

-- Paragraph 3: limited capability for work before 6th April 2026 and awaiting a further assessment (regulation 41(1)(b)); LCWRA determined on or after it.
-- src:2707 | This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2708 | (a) before 6th April 2026—
-- src:2709 | (i) the claimant has limited capability for work, and
-- src:2710 | (ii) in accordance with regulation 41(1)(b), the claimant is awaiting a further assessment under Part 5, and
-- src:2711 | (b) on or after 6th April 2026, the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element.
@ref Sch 5A para 3 (src:2707-2711)
DECLARE `Claimant with limited capability for work awaiting a further assessment` HAS
    `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant had limited capability for work`                                                       IS A DATE
    -- out of range: reg 41(1)(b) (piece uc4)
    `a day before 6th April 2026 on which, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(b), the claimant was awaiting a further assessment under Part 5`  IS A DATE
    `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element`  IS A DATE
    `the route by which that decision is made`                                                                                                IS A `Route by which a decision is made`

-- src:2707 | This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2708 | (a) before 6th April 2026—
-- src:2709 | (i) the claimant has limited capability for work, and
-- src:2710 | (ii) in accordance with regulation 41(1)(b), the claimant is awaiting a further assessment under Part 5, and
-- src:2711 | (b) on or after 6th April 2026, the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element.
@ref Sch 5A para 3 (src:2707-2711)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant with limited capability for work awaiting a further assessment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5A para 3 — limited capability for work and awaiting a further assessment before 6th April 2026` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant had limited capability for work` LESS THAN `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)
    AND (claimant's `a day before 6th April 2026 on which, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(b), the claimant was awaiting a further assessment under Part 5` LESS THAN `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)
    AND (claimant's `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element` AT LEAST `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)

-- Paragraph 4: LCWRA before 6th April 2026 but the award does not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1) (relevant period);
-- the element is included on or after it.
-- src:2713 | This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2714 | (a) before 6th April 2026—
-- src:2715 | (i) the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity, and
-- src:2716 | (ii) the claimant’s award of universal credit does not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1) (relevant period), and
-- src:2717 | (b) on or after 6th April 2026, the LCWRA element is included in the claimant’s award of universal credit.
@ref Sch 5A para 4 (src:2713-2717)
DECLARE `Claimant whose award does not include the LCWRA element on 6th April 2026` HAS
    `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant had limited capability for work and work-related activity`                           IS A DATE
    -- out of range: reg 28(1) (piece uc1)
    `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant's award did not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1) (relevant period)`  IS A DATE
    `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the LCWRA element is included in the claimant's award of universal credit`                  IS A DATE

-- src:2713 | This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2714 | (a) before 6th April 2026—
-- src:2715 | (i) the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity, and
-- src:2716 | (ii) the claimant’s award of universal credit does not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1) (relevant period), and
-- src:2717 | (b) on or after 6th April 2026, the LCWRA element is included in the claimant’s award of universal credit.
@ref Sch 5A para 4 (src:2713-2717)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant whose award does not include the LCWRA element on 6th April 2026`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5A para 4 — LCWRA before 6th April 2026 with the element left out by regulation 28(1)` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant had limited capability for work and work-related activity` LESS THAN `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)
    AND (claimant's `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant's award did not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1) (relevant period)` LESS THAN `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)
    AND (claimant's `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the LCWRA element is included in the claimant's award of universal credit` AT LEAST `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)

-- Paragraph 5: entitled to an employment and support allowance with the support component before 6th April 2026, and so entitled throughout the
-- period from 6th April 2026 to the date of an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element.
-- src:2719 | This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2720 | (a) before 6th April 2026, the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 that includes the support component within the meaning of that Part, and
-- src:2721 | (b) the claimant has been so entitled throughout the period beginning with 6th April 2026 and ending with the date on which the claimant is awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element.
@ref Sch 5A para 5 (src:2719-2721)
DECLARE `Claimant entitled to an employment and support allowance before 6th April 2026` HAS
    `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant was entitled to an employment and support allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 that includes the support component within the meaning of that Part`  IS A DATE
    `the claimant has been so entitled throughout the period beginning with 6th April 2026 and ending with the date on which the claimant is awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2719 | This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2720 | (a) before 6th April 2026, the claimant is entitled to an employment and support allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 that includes the support component within the meaning of that Part, and
-- src:2721 | (b) the claimant has been so entitled throughout the period beginning with 6th April 2026 and ending with the date on which the claimant is awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element.
@ref Sch 5A para 5 (src:2719-2721)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant entitled to an employment and support allowance before 6th April 2026`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5A para 5 — entitled to an employment and support allowance before 6th April 2026` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant was entitled to an employment and support allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 that includes the support component within the meaning of that Part` LESS THAN `Sch 5A — 6th April 2026`)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant has been so entitled throughout the period beginning with 6th April 2026 and ending with the date on which the claimant is awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 1: a claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity is a pre-2026 claimant if entitled to an award that includes the
-- LCWRA element by virtue of paragraph 2, 3, 4 or 5, and has been so entitled continuously since the element was included.
-- src:2697 | 1 Further circumstances in which a claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity is a “pre-2026 claimant” for the purposes of regulation 27
-- src:2698 | For the purposes of regulation 27, a claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity is a “pre-2026 claimant” if the claimant—
-- src:2699 | (a) is entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element by virtue of one of the following paragraphs, and
-- src:2700 | (b) has been so entitled continuously from the time that the LCWRA element was included in the award.
@ref Sch 5A para 1 (src:2697-2700)
DECLARE `Claimant who may be a pre-2026 claimant` HAS
    capability                                                                                                       IS A `Capability for work`
    `the claimant is entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant has been so entitled continuously from the time that the LCWRA element was included in the award`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `circumstances of paragraph 2`                                                                                   IS A `Claimant awaiting an assessment under Part 5`
    `circumstances of paragraph 3`                                                                                   IS A `Claimant with limited capability for work awaiting a further assessment`
    `circumstances of paragraph 4`                                                                                   IS A `Claimant whose award does not include the LCWRA element on 6th April 2026`
    `circumstances of paragraph 5`                                                                                   IS A `Claimant entitled to an employment and support allowance before 6th April 2026`

-- src:2699 | (a) is entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element by virtue of one of the following paragraphs, and
@ref Sch 5A para 1(a) (src:2699)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant who may be a pre-2026 claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5A para 1(a) — entitled to an award including the LCWRA element by virtue of one of paragraphs 2 to 5` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `the claimant is entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element`)
    AND (    (`Sch 5A para 2 — the claimant was awaiting an assessment before 6th April 2026 and is determined to have LCWRA on or after it` (claimant's `circumstances of paragraph 2`))
          OR (`Sch 5A para 3 — limited capability for work and awaiting a further assessment before 6th April 2026` (claimant's `circumstances of paragraph 3`))
          OR (`Sch 5A para 4 — LCWRA before 6th April 2026 with the element left out by regulation 28(1)` (claimant's `circumstances of paragraph 4`))
          OR (`Sch 5A para 5 — entitled to an employment and support allowance before 6th April 2026` (claimant's `circumstances of paragraph 5`)))

-- src:2697 | 1 Further circumstances in which a claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity is a “pre-2026 claimant” for the purposes of regulation 27
-- src:2698 | For the purposes of regulation 27, a claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity is a “pre-2026 claimant” if the claimant—
-- src:2699 | (a) is entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element by virtue of one of the following paragraphs, and
-- src:2700 | (b) has been so entitled continuously from the time that the LCWRA element was included in the award.
@ref Sch 5A para 1 (src:2697-2700)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant who may be a pre-2026 claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5A para 1 — the claimant is a pre-2026 claimant` claimant MEANS
    ((claimant's capability)'s `limited capability for work and work-related activity`)
    AND (`Sch 5A para 1(a) — entitled to an award including the LCWRA element by virtue of one of paragraphs 2 to 5` claimant)
    AND (claimant's `the claimant has been so entitled continuously from the time that the LCWRA element was included in the award`)
